 ; config.example.toml: test_w124_operator G10 reads it relative to the
 ; project root it resolves (the dune sandbox copy of lib/ makes that
 ; _build/default), so the file must be copied into the sandbox too.
 ; bin/main.ml: W124/W140 operator-audit tests open the CLI source at
 ; <project-root>/bin/main.ml. @runtest does not build bin/main.exe, so
 ; without this dep the file is missing from the sandbox and those tests
 ; Sys_error. The fleet runner uses --build-dir under /tmp, which cannot
 ; walk up to the real source tree.
 (deps (source_tree ../resources) ../config.example.toml ../bin/main.ml)
 (preprocess (pps lwt_ppx)))

; Standalone LIVE proof for the Core-parity reorg-depth-cap gating
; (Class-A fix): drives a real >288-deep reorg through Mining.submit_block ->
; Sync.reorganize. PRE-fix the deep reorg is refused (exit 1); POST-fix the
; archive node's tip flips to the heavier branch. Not part of the default
; test run (it builds two ~290-block chains); invoke explicitly:
;   dune exec test/test_deep_reorg_over_cap.exe
(executable
 (name test_deep_reorg_over_cap)
 (libraries camlcoin))

; Standalone LIVE proof that the reorg CONNECT path writes undo data that
; covers INTRA-BLOCK transaction chains (a tx spending an output created by an
; earlier tx in the SAME block). The reorg path used to rebuild undo from an
; overlay-then-disk reader, which cannot see the connecting block's own
; outputs, so List.filter_map silently dropped those prevouts and the undo
; came out SHORTER than the tx's input list -- which makes any later
; disconnect abort with "DisconnectBlock: tx and undo inconsistent".
; Ships with a CONTROL scenario (same block shape, txB spending a different
; on-disk coin) that must pass both pre- and post-fix.
; Not part of the default test run (it mines ~130 blocks across three
; branches, twice); invoke explicitly:
;   dune exec test/test_reorg_intrablock_undo.exe
(executable
 (name test_reorg_intrablock_undo)
 (libraries camlcoin))

; Standalone LIVE-REORG proof for txospender_index (the verifier walks a real
; reorg and checks the spender index agrees with the chain afterwards).
;
; This file existed from 2026-06-29 with NO dune stanza at all -- not excluded
; on purpose like the two above, which document their cost and give a `dune
; exec` line, but simply never wired in. It was therefore never COMPILED, let
; alone run, so nothing would have caught it bit-rotting against the library.
; Found 2026-08-30 by the #92 audit (how many test files does the suite
; actually execute?).
;
; Kept out of the default `tests` stanza for the same reason as its two
; neighbours -- it drives a live reorg and is slow. Invoke explicitly:
;   dune exec test/test_txospender_livereorg.exe
(executable
